<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! sense.kapae.mutes ~ a worldline branch sets aside, move-not-delete

Mutes a worldline branch (a fork-path-dead-end) and cascades the mute across a sensorium: the branch's turn-keys and every store's entries for them stop answering a recall. `sensorium` names the sensorium; absent, memory. Reversible, move-not-delete throughout: `sense.kapae.restores` brings the entries back, and the rows never leave.

The answer is {branch, muted_entries, resolved}; a branch no turn names answers `resolved: false` with nothing muted, never a phantom mute. The word names five doors in the house: this is the seat's branch mute, beside a wiki's promotion brake (`realm.kapae.raises`), a nexus quorum ban and a relation's marker. The terminal's `lares sense worldline kapae <branch>` names the same act and refuses honestly where its handle reads read-only; it joins this address as a cli skin when the sense door flips.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ a-branch

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`a-branch` params=`branch/<branch> tick/1 ~ mute one branch at a tick`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ branch · tick · sensorium

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`branch` params=`takes/branch-root needs/required ~ the worldline branch to mute, by the root turn-key of its fork`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`tick` params=`takes/whole-number needs/required ~ the tick the mute lands at; the restore names the same tick`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`sensorium` params=`takes/name ~ the sensorium to mute across; absent, memory`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ write

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`write` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ reversible and trusted: a move-not-delete mute the seat runs on the operator's loop`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ muted · unresolved

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`muted` params=`exit/0 fields/[[branch muted_entries resolved]] ~ the branch's turn-keys and each store's entries for them stand muted`>>
<<has entity=`band` name=`unresolved` params=`exit/0 ~ the branch names no turn; resolved reads false and nothing muted`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

